id=a52sxq_tethering
name=Galaxy A52s 5G netbpfload kernel 5.4 gate
author=kusti420
description=Google's Tethering APEX netbpfload refuses kernels < 5.10 (25Q4) / 5.15 (26Q4) and its services have reboot_on_failure -> bootloop. Run our own build of the AOSP loader (IchthysOS tree, 5.4 floor kept; build_netbpfload.sh) from /system: it reads BPF objects of both struct bpf_map_def layouts (192 bytes up to Tethering 26Q3, 180 since the 26Q4 train 373041100 - the layout change made the previous frozen Google binary SIGABRT -> reboot,bpfloader-failed -> apexd reverted every Play train since 2026-11-02), loads offload/test/clatd/dscpPolicy.o from the live APEX and netd.o from /system: a52_netd.<active Tethering versionCode>.o when the ROM ships one, else a52_netd.o (5.4 stats programs allowed at API >= 3610, BPF ringbuf maps created on 5.4 - needs the k4 ringbuf kernel; a52_netd.o also carries the maps Play train 372038420's userspace needs, a52_netd.373041100.o is that train's own netd.o since its map layouts differ). Google's original signed Tethering APEX ships untouched, so Google Play system updates can update it (IchthysOS-built modules carry SDK codename "Baklava" and are rejected by REL builds). TARGET_TETHERING_RESIGN_APEX=true restores the old re-signed APEX with the ringbuf users stubbed (kernels without ringbuf). Known 5.4 limits: the loaded {in,e}gress stats programs are the 5_4_t ones, so Local Network Protection (local_net maps, compat change 365139289 RESTRICT_LOCAL_NETWORK) and loopback cross-user isolation are not enforced. LNP is off in every known train; a 5.4 LNP program variant (is_system_or_root + ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK permission bit) is the plan for the train that turns it on, and k4-mainline-diag warns when it is on. Loopback isolation needs bpf_sk_lookup/sk_storage (5.10+ kernel).
